{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mw00/project-maya/pulls/622","id":5054724326,"node_id":"PR_kwDOU-xXos8AAAABLUj45g","html_url":"https://github.com/mw00/project-maya/pull/622","diff_url":"https://github.com/mw00/project-maya/pull/622.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/mw00/project-maya/pull/622.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mw00/project-maya/issues/622","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mw00/project-maya/pulls/622/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mw00/project-maya/pulls/622/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mw00/project-maya/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mw00/project-maya/issues/622/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mw00/project-maya/statuses/aed24df272c0f7f532b15edca2f796b9b6e5e29d","number":622,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"ds4 DSpark: the drafter head, markov steps and confidences only for the rows the round cut can keep (DS4_DSPARK_LAZY=0: all)","user":{"login":"SeriousRising","id":69419008,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5NDE5MDA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69419008?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeriousRising","html_url":"https://github.com/SeriousRising","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeriousRising/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeriousRising/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeriousRising/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeriousRising/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeriousRising/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeriousRising/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeriousRising/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeriousRising/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeriousRising/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**What.** Today `draft_()` (`src/ds4/ds4_model.cu:13792`, v1.1.35) runs the trunk's head over all 5 rows of the DSpark block, then 5 markov + argmax steps, then the confidence head for all 5 (`:13979`), and `round()` (`src/ds4/ds4_main.cpp:273`) throws away everything after the first cut confidence. In chat most rounds keep 0-2 drafts, so most of that head work (a 129280 x 5120 GEMV a row) is thrown away.\n\nWith this PR, when the head is on one device (no TP head group, no `DS4_DSPARK_DUMP`), `draft_()` works in up to three stages and evaluates `round()`'s own cut on the host after each:\n\n1. confidence 0 only (it reads `x_0` and `y`); if the first draft is cut, no head row runs at all;\n2. head rows 0-1, drafts 0-1, confidences 1-2;\n3. the remaining rows up to `min(block, DS4_DSPARK_MAX, room - 1)`.\n\nA stage runs only if every confidence so far passed. The host test is `round()`'s, with the same float operations in the same order (`h_w[k] >= conf_min && (cum *= h_w[k]) >= cum_min`). `Model::draft()` gets `max_n`, `conf_min`, `cum_min` and `min_n`; with the defaults (0) nothing is cut, so other callers keep the old behaviour.\n\nPrompt lookup: `round()` compares the lookup proposal with `drafts[0]` even when the drafter's first draft is cut, so the proposal is now made before `draft()`, and when there is one `min_n = 1` makes the lazy head produce row 0 anyway. `propose()` only reads the suffix table, so moving it earlier changes nothing.\n\n**Setting:** `DS4_DSPARK_LAZY` (read like `DS4_DSPARK_MAX` / `DS4_DSPARK_DUMP`), on by default because it gives the same drafts and is measured faster (below); `DS4_DSPARK_LAZY=0` = the full head, as before. A row in `docs/SETTINGS.md`.\n\n**Output: unchanged** (same drafts, same tokens):\n\n- `confidence_kernel` is one block per row and reads only `x_t` and `tok[t]`; `markov_add` and `sample_tokens` / `sample_draft` run per row exactly as before.\n- The GGUF head GEMV (`mv_kernel<kQ5_K, NC>` on this pack) computes each column with the same lanes, order and `warp_sum` whatever the launch's column count; only the 4 + 1 split of rows into launches becomes 2 + up to 3.\n- `round()` keeps the same count: the cut stops at the first failing confidence, at `room - 1`, or at the block.\n\n**Measured.** 2x NVIDIA CMP 170HX 64 GB (GA100, sm_80, CUDA 12.8; card 0 PCIe Gen2 x16, card 1 Gen2 x4: a mining card's link, platform-specific), 16-vCPU Xeon E5-2697 v4 VM, 106 GiB RAM. DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017 GSQ-RCO IQ2_XXS, layer split CUDA0 [0,20) / CUDA1 [20,40) + head, `--tp 1 --gpus 0,1 --dspark on --cpu-threads 14`.\n\nThe `maya-ds4` CLI on this branch, 2000 fixed prompt ids + 256 greedy tokens, `--suffix-draft 0`, one binary, one run each (a quick check):\n\n| | v1.1.35 | `DS4_DSPARK_LAZY=0` | default (lazy) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| token ids | (reference) | = v1.1.35 | = v1.1.35 |\n| DSpark rounds / offered / accepted, per-position counts | 80 / 194 / 175 | = v1.1.35 | = v1.1.35 |\n| drafting, ms a round | 6.28 | 6.27 | **5.38 (-14 %)** |\n| decode tok/s | 40.68 | 40.69 | 41.13 (+1.1 %) |\n\nWith prompt lookup on (`--suffix-draft 3`, and `DS4_ASYNC_T=16` from #608 so that a lookup window's rows do not depend on its size), `=0` and default give the same 256 ids (20 / 21 lookup rounds: the lookup's window choice follows wall-clock round times).\n\nEarlier, through the server on our v1.1.29-based fork (its other patches the same in both arms; 5 prompts x 512 tokens, temperature 0, thinking off; ms a verify window from the engine's timer; two repeats): lazy off 46.33 / 46.36 ms, 41.96 / 41.93 tok/s; lazy on **44.87 / 44.87 ms (-3.2 %)**, 43.32 / 43.32 tok/s; the same text hashes. The drafter there was 6.32 -> 5.40 ms a pass (5.00 -> 3.57 head rows a pass). Most of the saving is the head GEMV of rows the cut never keeps: the Q5_K head on dp4a costs ~0.68 ms a row on a CMP 170HX. Any single-device head should gain where the head GEMV is a visible share of a drafter pass; not measured on other GPUs. A TP head group / `mk_split` is unchanged (the lazy path is skipped).\n\n**Costs and limits.**\n\n- One extra D2H + sync (~30 µs) a drafter pass, and a third on passes that keep >= 2 drafts (~61 % of passes above); a net saving, as measured.\n- Not exercised: an EXL3 head (`fmt != 0`, split-K partials); the per-column argument was checked for the GGUF GEMV only. `DS4_DSPARK_LAZY=0` is the escape.\n- Not separately tested: `DS4_DSPARK_SAMPLE=1` at temperature > 0 (rows are drawn with the same per-row counter, so the draws should be the same).\n- `ds4_gguf_test` (full suite): ALL OK.\n\n**Checks** (as `.github/workflows/tests.yml`): `tools/check_hip_compat.py` OK; server tests 463 OK (12 skipped); installer and tools tests 584 OK (31 skipped) - the same counts as v1.1.35.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-28T17:20:44Z","updated_at":"2026-10-30T08:38:27Z","closed_at":"2026-10-30T08:38:27Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"SeriousRising:ds4-lazy-draft-head","ref":"ds4-lazy-draft-head","repo":{"id":1437354424,"node_id":"R_kgDOVaxJuA","name":"project-maya","full_name":"SeriousRising/project-maya","owner":{"login":"SeriousRising","id":69419008,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5NDE5MDA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69419008?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeriousRising","html_url":"https://github.com/SeriousRising","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeriousRising/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeriousRising/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeriousRising/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeriousRising/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeriousRising/subscriptions